  "question_stem": "The lifetimes, in hours, of a particular type of light bulb are normally distributed with mean 2000 hours and standard deviation $\\sigma$ hours. The probability that a randomly chosen light bulb of this type has a lifetime of more than 1800 hours is 0.96.",
